omx-panel (0.11.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Release 0.11.1: the changelog names the pages, the gestures and the
    static curve
  * docs: the renderer's input, and the changelog line (omx-panel#141)
  * 0.11.1: describe serves what the console's derivation served
  * test: describe over five descriptors as the desk's scan wrote them
  * describe: the symbols and params facts the console's derivation served
  * meaning-infer: a scanned control whose meaning is unknown is read; a Q at
    zero is no band's Q
  * docs/panel-layout.md: describe serves the facts the console's derivation
    served for a scanned descriptor
  * renderer: input answers with the control, its value and the gesture's
    begin and end, from schema/gestures.json (omx-panel#141)
  * docs/panel-gestures.md: the licence lines, and the console's table named
    in words (omx-panel#141)
  * gestures: the eq-marks MOD GUI face keeps its curve polyline and marks;
    the refusal is only of a widget named for a parameter (omx-panel#141)
  * gestures: the reference module, the docs and the fixtures' scripted
    gestures (omx-panel#141)
  * gestures: schema/gestures.json declares the table, the words and the
    timings; the widget enum grows to the panel-layout list (omx-panel#141)
  * docs: the pages are one cut (group whole, Easy first, remote pages as
    given), the skin's easy, describe --pages (omx-panel#143)
  * omx-panel describe --pages --per-page N serves the one cut to a surface
    that is not node; the fixtures' page sequence, the no-literal-width rule
    (omx-panel#143)
  * skin: the user's Easy list wins; describe passes the width and the remote
    pages to the one cut (omx-panel#143)
  * pagesOf is the one cut: Easy first, remote pages as given, a group kept
    whole at every width (omx-panel#143)
  * parity harness: the tolerance mode, held by value
  * MOD GUI static curve through omx-dsp's twin, with marks for declared
    origins
  * describe cuts the pages after the skin applies
  * describe serves the Easy controls
  * pagesOf: a control the values hide keeps its slot, blank

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Sat, 07 Nov 2026 18:27:12 +0000
